From a622fb0e17783a5f461c9ea1a2cdb6b91e024542 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devin Phat <devin.phat97@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 19:05:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: remove resources from state when Railway reports them
 missing

Terraform expects Read to call resp.State.RemoveResource when the remote
object no longer exists, so that the next plan recreates it. Every resource
in this provider returned a diagnostic error instead, which makes a refresh
fail permanently after an out-of-band deletion and breaks tooling built on
the provider (e.g. Crossplane/Upjet, whose observe step relies on removal
to detect both "not created yet" and "deleted").

- add isNotFoundError: true for Railway GraphQL errors whose message
  contains "not found" (Project/Environment/Service/... not found) and for
  helpers that wrap the new errNotFound sentinel
- project, environment, service, variable, variable_collection,
  shared_variable, custom_domain, service_domain, tcp_proxy: Read removes
  the resource from state on not found instead of erroring
- getVariable / getSharedVariable: return errNotFound when the key is
  missing instead of silently leaving stale state
- getVariableCollection: errNotFound when none of the variables exist
- readCustomDomain / findServiceDomain: wrap errNotFound
- tcp_proxy: remove from state when no proxy matches the stored id
- unit test for isNotFoundError
